## Step 1: First, calculate the number of apples left after using 20 to make lunch.
The school started with 38 apples. After using 20 to make lunch, they are left with 38 - 20 = 18 apples.

## Step 2: Then, add the number of apples bought to the number of apples left after using 20 to make lunch.
After buying 28 more apples, they have 18 + 28 = 46 apples.

